# Project Structure and Entry Points

- Refer to the architectural overview: [ARCHITECTURE.md](mdc:ARCHITECTURE.md)
- User documentation and setup: [README.md](mdc:README.md)

## Applet Basics
- **Applet ID**: `com.tim_willebrands.time_tracklet`
- **Binary name**: `cosmic-applet-clockify`
- **Desktop entry**: [cosmic-time-tracklet.desktop](mdc:cosmic-time-tracklet.desktop)

## Code Map
- Entrypoint: [src/main.rs](mdc:src/main.rs)
  - Calls `cosmic::applet::run::<Window>(())` to start the applet process.
- Applet model and UI: [src/window.rs](mdc:src/window.rs)
  - Implements `cosmic::Application` for `Window`.
  - Handles messages, popup lifecycle, and Clockify CLI calls.
- Wayland idle detection: [src/idle_monitor.rs](mdc:src/idle_monitor.rs)
  - Encapsulates `ext_idle_notifier_v1` and manages a background dispatch thread.
- Dependencies and features: [Cargo.toml](mdc:Cargo.toml)
  - Uses `libcosmic` with `applet`, `wayland`, `tokio` features.

## Runtime Model
- One applet process per panel instance (multi-monitor setups can launch multiple instances).
- UI runs on the COSMIC main thread; Wayland idle events are dispatched on a dedicated thread per instance.

## Common Tasks
- Build: `cargo build --release`
- Install binary: copy `target/release/cosmic-applet-clockify` to your system applet path.
- Register applet: install the desktop entry and add via COSMIC Settings.